Again, no, there isn't, or else even MC3 wouldn't be sufficient.  And
just because something is easy to get doesn't mean it's necessary--the
wishes in the castle wand are easy to get (if you can survive down to
it), but people *do* ignore them.  People do not regularly avoid
getting MC.  I do think it'd be an interesting challenge, especially in
the early game, because although there isn't much early on that's
affected by MC, a lot of the early equipment grants it, and would
therefore be off-limits; the latter-game attacks that are affected by
MC can generally be avoided with either E/Scare monster or genocide.

To sum up: MC is important, but is so easy to get that it's not worth
worrying about, though in the mid-game, it's good to do a paranoia
check to make sure you have some.  Is it as important as MR?  Probably
not, and since it's so easy to get, it's not worth worrying about.  But
there would be certain challenges to intentionally avoiding MC, which
might make it an interesting option for someone looking for a new
challenge.

